<section image-layout="blank"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item padding="32pt 48pt 22pt"><p role="eyebrow">Captain’s final position</p><h2>Two bearings test one cosmic history</h2><p font-size="18pt">Independent observations meet in an expansion-and-cooling model.</p><freeform-block w="840" h="248"><box type="content" x="0" y="8" w="315" h="94" sizing="fixed" background-color="surface" style="padding:14pt 18pt"><h3>Redshift</h3><p font-size="17pt">Distant galaxies’ light is stretched to longer wavelengths.</p></box><box type="content" x="0" y="145" w="315" h="94" sizing="fixed" background-color="surface" style="padding:14pt 18pt"><h3>Relic light</h3><p font-size="17pt">Cooled radiation preserves evidence of a hot early universe.</p></box><shape preset="rightArrow" x="330" y="48" w="95" h="22" fill="palette-2" stroke-width="0"/><shape preset="rightArrow" x="330" y="181" w="95" h="22" fill="palette-2" stroke-width="0"/><box type="content" x="445" y="38" w="375" h="170" sizing="fixed" background-color="surface" style="padding:20pt"><p role="eyebrow">The model they test</p><h3>Expansion + cooling</h3><p font-size="18pt">The universe changes with time. The model must account for both observations together.</p></box></freeform-block><p font-size="20pt"><b>No single blast port.</b> Large-scale expansion does not require a privileged center or an outer sea.</p><p role="caption">Observations → model → interpretation. A reasoning chart, not a literal map of the universe.</p></grid-item></grid></section>